<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lavr Kornilov</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lavr Kornilov was a Russian general who became commander-in-chief of the army in July 1917 and was accused of attempting a coup against the Provisional Government in the Kornilov affair that September. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a> he helped found the anti-Bolshevik <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> in the Don region and led its Ice March into the Kuban. He was killed by a shell during the assault on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a> in April 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lavr-kornilov.jpg" alt="Lavr Kornilov" width="320" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kornilov1916.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
